  "instance_name": "three_individuals",
  "label": "survivors of Auschwitz",
  "description": "Three emaciated, visibly traumatized individuals, likely Jewish Holocaust survivors, standing and sitting in front of a building. Their clothing is ragged and worn, indicating extreme suffering and deprivation. The image is a historical photograph colorized, and the overlaid text falsely claims they were liberated by the USSR in 1945, which is historically inaccurate as Auschwitz was liberated by the Soviet Red Army in January 1945, but the text misattributes the liberation to the USSR (which is correct but misleadingly framed). The individuals appear to be in a state of extreme physical and emotional distress, consistent with survivors of the Holocaust. Their presence is the central visual material and the subject of the meme's hateful intent, which seeks to trivialize their suffering by presenting the image as a 'colorized' novelty.",
